I go downstairs from my building.
Near my building, there is a small kirana store.
I go inside the store.
I have my shopping list in my hand.
The shopkeeper is a young man.
I politely say to him, "Bhaiya, namaste."
He smiles and says, "Namaste madam, tell me."
First, I ask for poha.
I say, "Please give me half a kilo of thick poha."
He weighs the poha and puts it in a paper bag.
Then, I look at my list again.
After that, I need peanuts.
I ask, "Do you have raw peanuts?"
He says, "Yes madam, how much do you need?"
I say, "Please give me a small packet of peanuts."
He gives me the packet.
I put both things in my cloth bag.
I pay him the money.
Now I need some fresh vegetables.
